diagInvariants -- ring of invariants of a diagonalizable group action
*********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        diagInvariants(T,U,R)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, whose rows are the values of the
        indeterminates under the torus action
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, whose rows are the values of the
        indeterminates under action of the finite group
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,  the basering
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * allComputations (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
      * grading (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note monomial subalgebra: MonomialSubalgebra,, the ring of
        invariants

Description
===========


This function computes the ring of invariants of a diagonalizable group D =
T\times G where T is a torus and G is a finite abelian group, both acting
diagonally on the polynomial ring K[X_1,\ldots,X_n]. The group actions are
specified by the input matrices M and N. The first matrix specifies the torus
action, the second the action of the finite group. See *note torusInvariants:
torusInvariants, or *note finiteDiagInvariants: finiteDiagInvariants, for more
detail. The output is the monomial subalgebra of invariants.


This method can be used with the options *note allComputations:
allComputations, and *note grading: grading,.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z,w];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : T=matrix({{-1,-1,2,0},{1,1,-2,-1}});                                    |
|                                                                             |
|              2       4                                                      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : U=matrix{{1,1,1,1,5},{1,0,2,0,7}}                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | 1 1 1 1 5 |                                                           |
|     | 1 0 2 0 7 |                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|              2       5                                                      |
|o3 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : diagInvariants(T,U,R)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}                         |
|                                        70 35     19 10   4 6 5   15 5 10    |
|                        generators => {y  z  , x*y  z  , x y z , x  y z  ,   |
|                        ring => R                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : MonomialSubalgebra of R                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                               }                             |
| 26 4 15   37 3 20   48 2 25   59   30   70 35                               |
|x  y z  , x  y z  , x  y z  , x  y*z  , x  z  }                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

