ehrhartRing(List,RingElement) -- Ehrhart ring
*********************************************

  * Function: *note ehrhartRing: ehrhartRing,
  * Usage: 
        ehrhartRing(L,t)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the monomials corresponding to the
        vertices of a lattice polytope
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,,  the free variable
        that should be used for the computation
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * allComputations (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note monomial subalgebra: MonomialSubalgebra,, generated by the
        lattice points of the polytope
      * a *note monomial subalgebra: MonomialSubalgebra,, the Ehrhart ring of
        the polytope

Description
===========


The exponent vectors of the given monomials are considered as vertices of a
lattice polytope P. The Ehrhart ring of a (lattice) polytope P is the monoid
algebra defined by the monoid of lattice points in the cone over the polytope
P; see Bruns and Gubeladze, Polytopes, Rings, and K-theory, Springer 2009, pp.
228, 229. The function returns two monomial subalgebras, the first has as
generators the monomials representing the lattice points of the polytope, the
second is the Ehrhart ring. If there is already a free variable in the original
ring (i.e. a variable that does not appear in any of the monomials in L), give
the function that variable as second input. The function then uses it instead
of creating a new one.
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/37[x,y,t];                                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : L={x^3, x^2*y, y^3, x*y^2};                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (A, B) = ehrhartRing(L, t);                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : A                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o4 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}     }     |
|                                        3     2   2    3       |
|                        generators => {y , x*y , x y, x }      |
|                        ring => R                              |
|                                                               |
|o4 : MonomialSubalgebra of R                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : B                                                         |
|                                                               |
|o5 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}          }|
|                                        3      2    2      3   |
|                        generators => {y t, x*y t, x y*t, x t} |
|                        ring => R                              |
|                                                               |
|o5 : MonomialSubalgebra of R                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

