finiteDiagInvariants -- ring of invariants of a finite group action
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        finiteDiagInvariants(U,R)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, whose rows are the values of the
        indeterminates under the action of a finite group
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,  the basering
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * allComputations (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
      * grading (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note monomial subalgebra: MonomialSubalgebra,, the ring of
        invariants

Description
===========


This function computes the ring of invariants of a finite abelian group G
acting diagonally on the surrounding polynomial ring K[X_1,\ldots,X_n]. The
group is the direct product of cyclic groups generated by finitely many
elements g_1,\ldots,g_w. The element g_i acts on the indeterminate X_j by
g_i(X_j)= \lambda_i^{u_{ij}}X_jwhere \lambda_i is a primitive root of unity of
order equal to ord(g_i). The ring of invariants is generated by all monomials
satisfying the system u_{i1}a_1+...+u_{in} a_n \equiv \ 0 mod ord(g_i),
i=1,\ldots,w. The input to the function is the w\times (n+1) matrix U with rows
u_{i1} \ldots u_{in} ord(g_i), i=1,\ldots,w. The output is the monomial
subalgebra of invariants R^G=\{f\in R : g_i f= f  for all i=1,\ldots,w\}.


This method can be used with the options *note allComputations:
allComputations, and *note grading: grading,.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z,w];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : U=matrix{{1,1,1,1,5},{1,0,2,0,7}}                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | 1 1 1 1 5 |                                                           |
|     | 1 0 2 0 7 |                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|              2       5                                                      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : finiteDiagInvariants(U,R)                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}                         |
|                                        5   7 3   14    35     4     7 2     |
|                        generators => {w , z w , z  w, z  , y*w , y*z w ,    |
|                        ring => R                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : MonomialSubalgebra of R                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                                             |
|   14   2 3   2 7    3 2   3 7   4    5     3      24       3   2 13   3 2   |
|y*z  , y w , y z w, y w , y z , y w, y , x*z w, x*z  , x*y*z , x z  , x z ,  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                                             |
| 5   4   5     3   5 2   2   5 3      5 4    7 3   7   2   7 2    7 3        |
|x z*w , x y*z*w , x y z*w , x y z*w, x y z, x w , x y*w , x y w, x y ,       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                 }                           |
| 12   2   12        12 2    14    14    19    35                             |
|x  z*w , x  y*z*w, x  y z, x  w, x  y, x  z, x  }                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

