getNumInvs -- returns the numerical invariants computed
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getNumInvs()
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, the numerical invariants

Description
===========


This function returns a hashtable containing the invariants printed to the file
with suffix inv, if the files are kept, i.e., if a filename is specified (see
*note Keeping results of the computation by Normaliz: Keeping results of the
computation by Normaliz,). The key of an entry is a *note String:
(Macaulay2Doc)String, describing the invariant, the value is the invariant,
namely an *note ZZ: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, for rank, index, multiplicity, a *note
Sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence, for the grading, the Hilbert series and the
Hilbert quasi-polynomial and a *note Boolean: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean, for graded
and primary (in the case of a Rees algebra).
