intersectionValRingIdeals -- intersection of valuation ideals
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        intersectionValRingIdeals(v,r)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, values of the indeterminates,
        the last column contains the lower bounds w_i
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,  the basering
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * allComputations (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
      * grading (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, the subalgebra and the
        generators of the module over it

Description
===========


A discrete monomial valuation v on R=K[X_1,\ldots,X_n] is determined by the
values v(X_j) of the indeterminates. This function takes as input the matrix
V=(v_i(X_j)), whose rows correspond to the values of the indeterminates for for
r valuations v_1, \ldots,v_r, with an additional column holding lower bounds
w_1,\ldots,w_r \in \ZZ. It returns the subalgebra S=\{f\in R: v_i(f)\geq 0,
i=1,\ldots,n\}, the intersection of the valuation rings of the r valuations,
and a system of generators of the S-submodule M=\{f\in R: v_i(f)\geq w_i,
i=1,\ldots,n\} over R, which consists of the elements whose i-th valuation is
greater or equal to the i-th bound w_i. If w_i>=0 for all i, then M is an ideal
in S.


This method can be used with the options *note allComputations:
allComputations, and *note grading: grading,. The additional data can be
accessed via the subalgebra in the *note HashTable: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z,w];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : V=matrix({{0,1,2,3,4},{-1,1,2,1,3}});                                   |
|                                                                             |
|              2       5                                                      |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : intersectionValRingIdeals(V,R)                                          |
|                                                                             |
|                                        3        2     2   2    2            |
|o3 = HashTable{"module generators" => {w , z*w, z , y*w , y w, y z, y        |
|               "subalgebra" => MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable        |
|                                                                             |
|                                                  generators => {w, z        |
|                                                  ring => R                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : HashTable                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|4     2     2      4                                                         |
| , x*z , x*y z, x*y }    }                                                   |
|{...1...}               }                                                    |
|                     2                                                       |
|, y, x*w, x*z, x*y, x z}                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note intersectionValRings: intersectionValRings, -- intersection of ring
    of valuations

