The generators of the integral closure of the Rees algebra of a monomial ideal.
*******************************************************************************


We use *note intclMonIdeal: intclMonIdeal, to compute the integral closure of a
monomial ideal and of its Rees algebra.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/37[x_1..x_7];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=ideal(x_1..x_6, x_1*x_2*x_3*x_7, x_1*x_2*x_4*x_7, x_1*x_3*x_5*x_7,    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1*x_4*x_6*x_7, x_1*x_5*x_6*x_7, x_2*x_3*x_6*x_7, x_2*x_4*x_5*x_7,          |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_2*x_5*x_6*x_7,x_3*x_4*x_5*x_7,x_3*x_4*x_6*x_7);                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (intcl,rees)=intclMonIdeal I;                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : intcl                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = ideal (x , x , x , x , x , x )                                          |
|             6   5   4   3   2   1                                           |
|                                                                             |
|              ZZ                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of --[x ..x , a]                                                  |
|              37  1   7                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : rees                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}                         |
|                        generators => {x , x , x a, x , x a, x , x a, x ,    |
|                                        7   6   6    5   5    4   4    3     |
|                                ZZ                                           |
|                        ring => --[x ..x , a]                                |
|                                37  1   7                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                           ZZ                                                |
|o5 : MonomialSubalgebra of --[x ..x , a]                                     |
|                           37  1   7                                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                      }                                                      |
|x a, x , x a, x , x a}                                                       |
| 3    2   2    1   1                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+


The first entry is an ideal, the integral closure of the original ideal, the
second one a monomial subalgebra. Each variable in the example appears in a
generator of the ideal. Therefore an auxiliary variable a is added to the ring.
If there were a free variable in the ring, say x_8, then one can give this
variable as a second argument to the function, which then is used as auxiliary
variable.
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R=ZZ/37[x_1..x_8];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : I=ideal(x_1..x_6, x_1*x_2*x_3*x_7, x_1*x_2*x_4*x_7, x_1*x_3*x_5*x_7,    |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : Ideal of R                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_1*x_4*x_6*x_7, x_1*x_5*x_6*x_7, x_2*x_3*x_6*x_7, x_2*x_4*x_5*x_7,          |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|x_2*x_5*x_6*x_7,x_3*x_4*x_5*x_7,x_3*x_4*x_6*x_7);                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : (intcl,rees)=intclMonIdeal(I,x_8);                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : intcl                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = ideal (x , x , x , x , x , x )                                          |
|             6   5   4   3   2   1                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : rees                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o10 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}                        |
|                         generators => {x , x , x x , x , x x , x , x x , x ,|
|                                         7   6   6 8   5   5 8   4   4 8   3 |
|                         ring => R                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : MonomialSubalgebra of R                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                         }                                                   |
|x x , x , x x , x , x x }                                                    |
| 3 8   2   2 8   1   1 8                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

