File: Normaliz.info, Node: torusInvariants, Next: vars_lpMonomialSubalgebra_rp, Prev: The lattice points_cm Ehrhart series and the support hyperplanes of an integral polytope_pd, Up: Top

torusInvariants -- ring of invariants of torus action
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        torusInvariants(T,R)
  * Inputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, matrix (a_{ij}) of the action
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,  the ring on which the action takes
        place
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * allComputations (missing documentation) => ..., default value false, 
      * grading (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note monomial subalgebra: MonomialSubalgebra,, the ring of
        invariants R^T

Description
===========


 Let T=(K^*)^r be the r-dimensional torus acting on the polynomial ring
R=K[X_1,\ldots,X_n] diagonally. Such an action can be described as follows:
there are integers a_{ij}, i=1,\ldots,r, j=1,\ldots,n, such that
(\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_r)\in T acts by the substitution

X_j\mapsto \lambda_1^{a_{1j}}*\ldots*\lambda_r^{a_{rj}}X_j,    j=1,\ldots,n.

The function takes the matrix (a_{ij}) as input and computes the ring of
invariants R^T=\{f\in R: \lambda f=f for all \lambda \in T\}.


This method can be used with the options *note allComputations:
allComputations, and *note grading: grading,.
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[x,y,z,w];                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : T=matrix({{-1,-1,2,0},{1,1,-2,-1}});               |
|                                                        |
|              2       4                                 |
|o2 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                  |
+--------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : torusInvariants(T,R)                               |
|                                                        |
|o3 = MonomialSubalgebra{cache => CacheTable{...1...}   }|
|                                        2           2   |
|                        generators => {y z, x*y*z, x z} |
|                        ring => R                       |
|                                                        |
|o3 : MonomialSubalgebra of R                            |
+--------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note finiteDiagInvariants: finiteDiagInvariants, -- ring of invariants of
    a finite group action
  * *note diagInvariants: diagInvariants, -- ring of invariants of a
    diagonalizable group action

Ways to use torusInvariants:
============================

  * "torusInvariants(Matrix,Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note torusInvariants: torusInvariants, is a *note method function
with options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

